All save rates are assumptions, deliberately at or below the 30% convention of profit-based churn studies [[verbeke2012](references.md#verbeke2012), [verbraken2013](references.md#verbraken2013)], because field experiments show offers can be ineffective or even raise churn for high-risk customers [[ascarza2018](references.md#ascarza2018), [ascarza2016](references.md#ascarza2016)]. Each offer is a separate arm in the pilot.

## Design parameters (policy choices, not estimates)

| Parameter | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Default budget | {{ cfg.campaign.budget_share | pct(0) }} of customers x standard offer ({{ budget.base | usd }} for {{ budget.n_test | num }} customers) | The business question fixes a budget; the team set it as a share of customers so a manager can scale it with the customer base. It is a starting point, not a recommendation |
| Contact cap | {{ cfg.campaign.max_contact_share | pct(0) }} of customers per wave | Customer-experience guardrail against over-contacting |
| Strategy selection | Segment offers only if they beat the single offer by >= {{ cfg.campaign.strategy_selection.min_relative_gain | pct(0) }} on validation | Prefer the simpler policy unless the gain is material |
| Budget recommendation | Largest budget whose last step earns >= {{ cfg.campaign.recommendation.min_marginal_roi | pct(0) }} marginal ROI, chosen on validation | A management minimum return on marketing spend; time value is already in the discounted customer value, so the hurdle only stops spending where the next dollar barely pays |
| Value horizon cap | {{ cfg.value.horizon_cap_months }} months | Upper bound on remaining months whatever the horizon and factors |
| Tenure factors | new {{ cfg.value.tenure_factors.new }}, developing {{ cfg.value.tenure_factors.developing }}, loyal {{ cfg.value.tenure_factors.loyal }} | Retention rises with tenure [faderhardie2010]; the factors themselves are a team assumption |
| Risk / value cut-offs | {{ cfg.segments.high_risk_quantile | pct(0) }} percentiles on validation (risk {{ thresholds.risk | num(3) }}, value {{ thresholds.value | usd }}) | Defines the high-risk/high-value segment used in coverage |
| Fairness review band | selection-rate ratio outside {{ cfg.guardrails.selection_ratio_alert[0] }}-{{ cfg.guardrails.selection_ratio_alert[1] }}, group >= {{ cfg.guardrails.min_group_size }} customers | Four-fifths screen used as an analogy [cfr1607] |
| Pilot | alpha {{ cfg.pilot.alpha }}, power {{ cfg.pilot.power | pct(0) }}, {{ cfg.pilot.holdout_share | pct(0) }} holdout, {{ cfg.pilot.outcome_window_days }}-day outcome | Standard two-arm test design [kohavi2020] |

## Change control

Change values only in `configs/default.yaml`, then run `python -m telco_retention run-all`. The run manifest stores the full configuration, so every report, figure and dashboard default can be traced to the assumptions it used. Replace assumptions with measured values as soon as the pilot produces them (owner named in the first table).
